- **Data Storage:** Verify if text files adequately cover all necessary data. If additional functionalities are introduced (like user roles, item categories), make sure to adapt the file structures accordingly. Consider standardizing the format for lines in the files, such as ensuring consistency in delimiters or including versioning if data schema changes.

- **Data Structures:** Maintain single responsibility across classes. Each class should have a focused scope, ensuring that `UserManager` manages only user-related logic and `ItemManager` focuses solely on item management. If more functionality develops, consider creating separate classes to handle responsibilities like validation or reporting.
